    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="d305-01" n="1" xml:id="d305-01"/>

                <head>305. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger) to Secretary
                    of State Rogers and the
                    Director of the Arms Control and Disarmament Agency
                        (Smith)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d305-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d305-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1971-11-17"
                        >November 17, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Clearance of Statements and Instructions Concerning Nuclear Test Ban
                        Policy</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has directed that official statements and instructions to
                    delegations at the United Nations and the Conference of the Committee on
                    Disarmament concerning U.S. nuclear test ban policy will be cleared at the White
                    House.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        Henry A. Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d305-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d305-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 229, Agency Files, Department of Defense, volume 14,
                    Nov–Dec 1971. Confidential. A copy was sent to Laird, Schlesinger, and
                        Moorer.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d305-f2" n="2" xml:id="d305-f2-content">
                <p>The President issued directions for clearance of statements and instructions
                    concerning nuclear test ban policy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
